{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact 1c802763fbd061650051d56752bf1e06701f6254, tree df943f5bd9055cc8be0b9922cb076d03bfee575f, primary34759207 with both current artifacts. Draft3's dynamic act tools follow Hugh's new direction. The earlier security corrections are materially addressed at design level; they are not implementation acceptance. The retired8db invitation received no verdict, and its verified unchanged Source is carried explicitly.\n\nArchitecture: one generated service is still a useful direction. Founding, beside inputs and the unfamiliar application witness improve completeness. The shared-name descriptor contract, native capability preparation and discovery roots remain incomplete.\n\nSecurity: required caller-known keys, intentional credential output, judge-only diagnostics, Origin rejection and launch-bearer isolation resolve the earlier direct contradictions. Descriptor-to-target binding and retained terminal outcomes still need correction. Native judgment prevents a forged grant but cannot repair a tool that signs a different contract from the one its caller read.\n\nSimplification: direct verbs remove the indirection Hugh identified. Keep that result while specifying variants, modes, discovery and continuations. Do not make the generic fallback silently necessary for the default surface, or satisfy bounds by losing valid acts and fields.\n\nRequired corrections:\n\n1. [P2] Bind a generated tool to the exact target declaration (section3, about143-174). Same-name definitions share one tool, but each promises its own fields, guards and schema. Native change.json and change3.json both have name change and the same profile: propose-manifest has incompatible field sets (old base/complete/decisions/instance/integration/selected/tree and optionals; new base/files). One arbitrary change.propose-manifest schema either rejects valid input or advertises different meaning. Preserve the short-name direction with explicit digest variants, a target/digest-discriminated union or another unambiguous target-bound descriptor. Check the definition name and exact retained digest before a new preparation; checking only that kind exists also allows a different-name same-kind target. Stale descriptors must refresh without signing; retained replays use their original binding. Namespace routing/custody/beside controls separately from arbitrary declared fields, and derive on for every step/subject form, not only transitions. Witness incompatible same-name definitions, inactive old lanes, different-name same-kind targets, reserved field-name collisions and activation with a cached descriptor.\n\n2. [P2] Account for the native preparation/read surface in W1 (section3 submit path and W1). FULL native contract/transport.ts exposes prepare(scope,signed,grants,capability,step) separately from submit. The tool tables declare envelope preparation followed by submit, but give no capability/step dispatch path. State the generic mechanism, tied to the original signed meaning/custody, and show the tools for Git/hold capability preparation. Explicitly map canonical log, outbox and duty reads as well: verification and send-outcome workflows need their complete native data, not only a summarized history line or duty ID. Existing generic tools may compose these if the inventory demonstrates that. This is a completeness requirement, not an application-specific adapter request.\n\n3. [P2] Define authoritative discovery and invalidation (section3 listed/changes; section6 standing). A newly founded standalone scope adds tools, yet the listed discovery sources are repository platform/active/lane definitions. A second or restarted connection has no specified source for that standalone scope, contradicting same-key/same-room equality independent of connection history. Define the durable inventory/configured roots and per-target authority sources, including an existing non-repository Counter and mixed memberships. Unknown standing is handled only by acts/act, which the default hides; specify its default behavior without treating unreadable standing as a denial or a grant. A server that refreshes only during calls cannot notify an idle host of external activation while that host waits for list_changed. Specify a bounded watch/poll/invalidation mechanism and account for its reads. Paginated tools/list needs a stable generation/cursor or an explicit restart rule across role/definition changes. Witness two connections, reconnect, external idle activation, mixed authority and pagination during change.\n\n4. [P2] Reconcile default and fallback modes (sections3,6,9, W1/W7). The default correctly hides acts/act, but canonical activity recipes and standing-refresh examples still require them. Rewrite default compositions with generated act tools. Define whether --generic replaces or adds dynamic tools, including the promised tool-count-limited-host use, and which discovery/invocation paths are available in each mode. W1/W2 must prove default functionality without hidden fallback calls and equivalent complete functionality in generic mode. Correct stale cross-references, including the section14 token-gate wording now replaced by Hugh's newer decision.\n\n5. [P2] Preserve terminal outcomes and correct expiry semantics (section7 same-meaning/archive/expiry). Same-meaning retries are unconditionally resent, including archived refused records. Native derive/fold indexes accepted sealed acts, not refusals; an unexpired previously refused envelope can later accept when mutable authority/guards change. Returning the recorded refusal should not silently become fresh work. Distinguish prepared/sent/unknown recovery from accepted/refused terminal replay; return the retained answer, or make deliberate original replay a separately explicit caller-authorized operation while retaining both outcomes. The universal claim that expired replay answers expired and resolves it is false: native derive/judge checks matching accepted actor/key+intent digest BEFORE notAfter, and core.settle reads the original receipt without expiry or a turn. Accepted-but-lost replay can return that receipt; submit can also remain unavailable before receipt lookup due to timed drain. Only an actually definitive same-scope/incarnation result resolves unknown; not-found is not a historical refusal. W6 needs accepted reply loss then expiry, unknown/unavailable retention, and a terminal refusal followed by changed authority, with no automatic new key.\n\n6. [P2] Keep complete output representable under the proposed bounds (sections4,7,9). State whether 256KiB is a list response-page bound or an aggregate gate, and how every valid tool/schema remains available when the list or a single schema exceeds the gate. Paging merely where a host supports it does not specify tools/list traversal or preserve a too-large individual schema. Long guards and the names of omitted guards also need a bounded truthful pointer that does not contradict the 1000-character description gate. Bound idempotency-key UTF-8 length and diagnostics; any unique string plus oldest-key error lists can exceed a 4KiB response. Define custody record/store byte limits, atomic archival and bounded/indexed archive lookup without deleting unresolved envelopes. Retain the improved whole-response, cold/fallback and child-in-wait accounting; W5 measures the complete defined behavior, not a truncated fixed fixture.\n\n7. [P2] Separate the two MCP wire revisions truthfully (newsection7 and W7). 2026-07-28 does not negotiate at initialize: it removed the initialize/initialized handshake and protocol sessions, carries version/capabilities per request, and requires server/discover. Tool-list change delivery uses opted-in subscriptions/listen, not a notification piggybacked on any unrelated tool response. Define that modern path separately from 2025-11-25 initialization/session/GET compatibility; the older specification permits sessions rather than requiring every server to issue one. The minimal-handler alternative must implement the selected revision's methods instead of only initialize/ping/tools-list/call. W7 should drive real clients for both wire revisions, including modern first request without initialize, discovery, version mismatch and subscribed changes, while preserving equivalent native outcomes and actor isolation. Sources: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/blob/main/docs/specification/2026-07-28/changelog.mdx and https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-11-25/basic/transports . Supporting both revisions is the requested outcome; simulating the old handshake for the modern client does not achieve it.\n\nCoverage: Root FULL-read8db BODY56120B/12 contiguous spans; all four final analyses/audits FULL; native peer BODY/U3 and outcome units independently verified, with prior contract/derive/runtime authorities blob-identical through1c. Root FULL-read corrected7576B8db-to1c U3 in4000/3576B spans and the added body regions; unchanged line regions inherit exact prior coverage. Initial oversized/truncated delta got zero credit and was reread bounded. 1c BODY58795B SHA76e40bdb8f03c0102cb0414fcffaf51ddc1e01f0be37eae16e27a3a4dc93daff; auditmcp031-1c-native-coverage-audit.json SHA932b0e9b9cd6f4f656a4eaf9518ddb3f7221a0cf21abeb49041c52ef8ebf097a. README's updated entry/U3 were read; unchanged whole715k index is not claimed FULL or blanket-approved. Real-definition field comparison is a bounded native data projection, not whole-definition FULL credit. Outcome helper's accidental generated/truncated probe got zero authority credit and was corrected to bounded authored Source. No Source/test/gate/build/install, private program/log/credential, browser or provider execution by checker. W1-W7 remain prospective implementation witnesses. Normal prepare binds only design2c3832/promise059afc; no implementation, hosted/native acceptance or broad original MCP outcome closes through this verdict.","body":{"ar